  "corpus_documents": [
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 1,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Reading notes: the original 2014 study reported an effect size of 0.48, on 240 undergraduates at one university.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Noted. Worth checking what the confidence interval was before treating that as the reference value.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-09-02T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "effect-size"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 2,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "The replication: the 2019 replication found an effect size of 0.21, less than half the original. The interval excludes the original estimate.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "So the disagreement is not just about power. That is the part the commentaries will focus on.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-09-09T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "replication"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 3,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Scale of the replication: the replication used 1,842 participants across nine sites.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Nine sites is enough to look at between-site variation, which the original could not.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-09-16T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "methods"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 4,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Funding note: the Vestrand Foundation funded both the original study and the replication. That answers the obvious objection about adversarial replication.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the funding argument cuts the other way from how it is usually used.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-09-23T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "funding"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 5,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Methods comparison: both studies used the same 14-item attention scale, administered in the same order.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "So an instrument difference cannot explain the gap.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-10-07T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "methods"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 6,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Commentary: Ohlsson argues the replication changed the incentive structure of the task. His claim is that the payment schedule made the task easier to satisfice.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "That is testable against the per-site data, if they released it.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-10-14T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "critique"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "ohlsson-exchange"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 7,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Reply published: the replication authors answered that the incentive change was pre-registered and appears in the accepted protocol.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the objection is about whether the change was wise, not whether it was hidden.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-10-21T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "critique"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "ohlsson-exchange"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 8,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Site-level detail: the Bergen site alone reported an effect size of 0.51, close to the original.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "One site matching the original is what you would expect from sampling variation alone, so it is weak evidence on its own.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-11-04T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "sites"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 9,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Also: three sites were excluded from the pooled estimate for protocol deviations. The pooled figure is over six sites, not nine.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "That is worth stating whenever the 0.21 is quoted.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-11-18T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "sites"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 10,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Attrition: dropout was 11% in the replication and 4% in the original.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Higher but not alarming, and it is in the direction the online format would predict.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-12-02T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "methods"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 11,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Meta-analysis: the 2022 meta-analysis pooled 31 studies and reported 0.26, with substantial heterogeneity.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "So the pooled estimate sits between the two, closer to the replication.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2025-12-16T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "meta"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "meta-analysis"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 12,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Context: pre-registration became a journal requirement in 2018, which is after the original and before the replication.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "That explains why only one of the two has an accepted protocol to point at.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2026-01-13T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "norms"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "meta-analysis"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 13,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Instrumentation: all sites ran the task in the same open-source presentation software, version-pinned.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Then timing differences between sites are hardware, not software.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2026-01-27T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "methods"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "attention-effect"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 14,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Draft argument: the original is the outlier, not the replication.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "The meta-analytic estimate supports that reading, and the single-site match does not undercut it.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2026-02-10T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "writing"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "review-paper"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 15,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "New evidence: a 2025 registered report with 4,100 participants reported 0.19, the largest sample so far.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "That moves the pooled estimate down again and is hard to dismiss on power.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2026-03-03T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "effect-size"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "meta-analysis"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 16,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Reviewer question: how many participants in total across the replication and the 2025 registered report?",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Add the two numbers reported in the notes rather than quoting either alone.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2026-03-17T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "writing"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "review-paper"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 17,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Decision: the review will report a range rather than a point estimate.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Given the heterogeneity that is the defensible choice.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2026-04-07T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "writing"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "review-paper"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "corpus_document_id": 18,
      "document_content": [
        {
          "text": "Submitted. The funding and pre-registration notes are in the limitations section.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "user"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Good. Those are the two things a reader will otherwise ask about.",
          "labels": {
            "role": "assistant"
          }
        }
      ],
      "document_metadata": {
        "recorded_at": "2026-04-21T00:00:00Z",
        "topics": [
          "writing"
        ],
        "threads": [
          "review-paper"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
